  <h1>How to Identify Spam Calls & Protect Yourself in India (2026 Guide)</h1>
  
  <div class="meta">
    <span>🗓️ August 2026</span>
    <span>⏱️ 5 min read</span>
    <span>✍️ Mobile No Track Team</span>
  </div>

  <p>Spam calls, telemarketing, and digital fraud calls have become a major daily nuisance. Scammers constantly use phone number spoofing, automated robocalls, and urgent threats to trick people.</p>

  <p>This guide explains how to identify suspicious phone calls and what official steps you can take to stop them.</p>

  <div class="summary-box">
    <strong>One-line summary:</strong> Never share OTPs or bank details over the phone. Report fraudulent callers directly to TRAI (DND 1909) or the Cybercrime Helpline (1930).
  </div>

  <h2>Common Types of Scam Calls in India</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>⚠️ Fake Bank / KYC Scams</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 13px; margin:0;">Callers pretending to be bank staff asking you to update KYC or share OTPs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>📦 Courier / Customs Fraud</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 13px; margin:0;">Claims that a illegal package in your name was intercepted by customs or police.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>⚡ Electricity Bill Scams</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 13px; margin:0;">Urgent messages threatening power disconnection if a payment isn't made immediately.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>💼 Job Offer Frauds</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 13px; margin:0;">Promises of part-time online tasks requiring upfront registration fees.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>4 Essential Steps to Stop Unwanted Calls</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Activate Do Not Disturb (DND):</strong> Send an SMS with <code>START 0</code> to <strong>1909</strong> to register on TRAI's National Customer Preference Register.</li>
    <li><strong>Use Sanchar Saathi (Chakshu Portal):</strong> Report suspect fraud communications on DoT's official website (sancharsaathi.gov.in/sfc).</li>
    <li><strong>Report Cyber Crime:</strong> If you lost money, immediately call <strong>1930</strong> or register a complaint at <strong>cybercrime.gov.in</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Never Click Unknown Links:</strong> Do not open links sent via SMS from unknown numbers claiming urgent account updates.</li>
  </ul>

